Absolutely. Below is the complete standalone implementation, organized file-by-file so you can copy it directly into a small Maven project.

The tool will:

Accept Directory 1 and Directory 2 from command line.

Recursively scan .java files.

Detect DTOs based on configurable suffixes.

Parse Java using JavaParser.

Ignore class/package names for the primary comparison.

Compare field names + field types.

Handle field order differences.

Calculate similarity.

Run comparisons in parallel.

Avoid an expensive full N × M comparison by using field-count candidate grouping.

Generate:

.csv

.xlsx


Put the reports in an output directory.

Include exact matches, similar matches, and unmatched DTOs.

Show which fields differ.



