15. One thing I would change depending on your codebase

Right now DTO detection is:

return name.endsWith("dto")
        || name.endsWith("request")
        || name.endsWith("response")
        || name.endsWith("model");

If your project has packages such as:

model
request
response
dto

we can make this much more accurate by detecting DTOs based on:

package name

class name

Lombok annotations

Jackson annotations

Spring annotations

whether the class contains only fields/getters/setters

whether it extends another DTO

Java record

nested DTOs


That would reduce false positives substantially.


